In short: Capri is free and stays free. You can use her, change her and share what you made, as long as nobody
pays for it. The full terms below are the ones that count.

1. WHAT THIS LICENSE COVERS

   This license covers the source code and the documentation written for this project (the "Software"). It does
   not cover the elements listed in section 6.

2. WHAT YOU MAY DO

   Provided you follow the conditions below, you may, free of charge:
   a) use the Software for any non-commercial purpose (personal, hobby, study, research, education, non-profit);
   b) copy it and share it with others;
   c) modify it and share your modified versions.

3. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

   You may not sell the Software, nor anything made from its source code, and you may not use it to make money.
   This includes, for example: selling or renting copies, license keys, subscriptions, paid access or paid
   features, paid orders or commissions, paid hosting or services built on it, bundling it in a paid product, and
   any use that brings you advertising or sponsorship revenue because of the Software.

   Donations that give nothing in return are allowed, as long as they do not unlock anything.

4. CONDITIONS

   a) Keep this license file and the copyright line "Copyright (c) 2026 Cellri131" in every copy you share.
   b) Clearly state that you changed the Software if you share a modified version, and do not present it as the
      original or as an official version.
   c) Share your modified versions under these same terms, free of charge.
   d) Do not remove or hide the fan project notice (section 7).

5. YOUR OWN CONTRIBUTIONS

   What you write yourself and add to the Software belongs to you, but when you share it together with the
   Software it follows these same terms.

6. WHAT THIS LICENSE DOES NOT COVER

   a) The character artwork: the images in "assets/" and "docs/images/", and the icon files ("Icon*.png",
      "*.ico"). They show the character Capri from "Cyberpunk: Edgerunners" and belong to their respective rights
      holders (CD PROJEKT RED, Studio Trigger and others). No right over them is granted here.
   b) The voice file "capri_french.safetensors" and the models downloaded by third-party tools (Pocket-TTS, Piper
      voices). They keep their own licenses.
   c) Third-party libraries and tools (see "requirements.txt"). They keep their own licenses.

7. FAN PROJECT

   This is an unofficial fan project. It is not affiliated with, nor endorsed by, CD PROJEKT RED, Studio Trigger
   or Netflix.

8. END OF THE LICENSE

   If you break these terms, your rights end. If you are told in writing and fix the problem within 30 days, they
   are restored. Otherwise they end for good. The author may also give you separate permission in writing, for
   example for commercial use.

9. NO WARRANTY

   THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED
   TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL
   THE AUTHOR BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR
   OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE
   SOFTWARE.

